title: Query
kind: overview
aliases: queries dsl normal-dsl focus-query
summary: A query selects metarecords by their fields — values, presence, references and trees — written in the DSL or the simplified language.

Most things that list metarecords are driven by a ''query'': a filter selecting
which ones appear — the GUI's lists, `mf metarecord -q`, the writes over a set. An
empty query matches everything.

There are two languages. The ''DSL'' is precise:

```
rating > 3 AND genre = "jazz"
mfr_path ->* "/music/jazz" AND title MATCHES "[Ll]ive"
tag -> (path =>* "music/jazz")
```

The ''simplified'' language is shorter, forgiving and configurable; it expands into
the DSL on the client, and is what the GUI's query box takes by default (`mf … -s`
on the command line). The notes here describe the DSL; the other has its own: [[Simplified query language]].

Both compile to one JSON form ([[Query IR]]), which is what the daemon evaluates —
from its store's bitmaps, never in SQL ([[Query engine]]).

